  "prefLabel": "He-M 513.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2020-06-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-M 513.01 Purpose. The purpose of these rules is to establish standards for respite services as part of a system of community based services and supports responsive to the changing needs of individuals with developmental disabilities or acquired brain disorders and their families. These rules also apply to children, birth through age 2, and their families who are eligible for family-centered early supports and services.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for He-M 513) #4495, eff 9-23-88; EXPIRED: 9-23-94\n\nNew. #6155, eff 12-29-95; ss by #8016, eff 12-29-03; ss by #10030, eff 12-1-11, EXPIRED: 12-1-19\n\nNew. #12944, INTERIM, eff 12-20-19, EXPIRED: 6-17-20\n\nNew. #13263, eff 9-22-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-m500.html"
